Buffered Reader and Scanner both use Sequential Access, meaning they go through from
start to finish, line by line within the memory

Cache is used for temporary storage to prevent data from being moved over a long distance
Cache is a hardware limitation, not a software limitation

Disk is a lot slower to run than Memory

Sequential Access requires reading through and writing out an entire piece of data

Random Access uses a hard disk to treat data like an array and using base offset calculation 
to locate the specified portion

Delimiters will not be necessary for Random Access

For Random Access you need to designate a set limit for data storage when making records

int userID - 4 bytes
String username - 15 bytes
String passwd - 20 bytes

Record Length - 4 + (15 + 20) * 2 = 74 bytes

In this example, the offset will be the base times the Record Length
The File Pointer will use this to find one particular record  within the memory

if you wanted to sort through a Random Access File by name, you'd need an Index File that would provide the name
and the offset value with that name's record, in order for you to do a search utilizing the index File to find the Name's record
to access and read